The Thread of Fate, They Say

[Stanza 1]
A garden of flowers, with a heart in my hand that beats for you
Can we let our lips talk without us uttering a word?
The shower of love washing away the tears 
Is this the Thread of Fate they talk about?

[Stanza 2]
Strange, isn’t it? Trying to find my answers in you
Then, why do I find my shadow lost in the mist of the unknown?
Behind my eyelids, there’s a world I see, staring into your void-like eyes 
Is it the Thread of Fate they talk about, or is it all in my head? 

[Stanza 3]
If you aren’t the paint on my canvas
Then why do I see you in the flowers around me?
You are more captivating than all shades of purple 
But the Thread of Fate is red, they say, don’t they?

[Stanza 4]
Between our eyes is where my soul breathes
And as the ink on your pages is where my destiny lies
Would you hold me until the flowers wither, the colors fade away?
Do you believe in the Thread of Fate they talk about?
